On 6/8/05, Robin Lee Powell <rlpowell@digitalkingdom.org> wrote:

> zvati is:
> 
> x1 (object/event) is at/attending/present at x2 (event/location)
> 
> Events are situated in time.

In time and space, like every other spatio-temporal object.
An event has a duration (which can be specified with ze'a)
and a spatial extension (specifiable with ve'a). It also has
a position in time (specifiable with ca) and a position in
space (specifiable with bu'u).

If I say {mi zvati lo nu do tavla}, that means that I am
present at your talk, i.e. in the same place where
your talk takes place.

mu'o mi'e xorxes


